# Throwaway diagnostics. A session's probes get named *-tmp.* and live in the tree only while
# they run; ignoring them keeps `git add -A` from sweeping one into a commit, which has happened.
#
# Enumerate the EXTENSIONS, not the guesses. This list was three specific spellings, and the first
# probe of 2026-08-08 was an ESM TypeScript file named `*-tmp.mts` — an obvious choice, and not one
# of them. `MAINTAINING.md` says to check the glob covers the name you chose; making the glob cover
# the names anyone would choose is the cheaper half of that.
*-tmp.mjs
*-tmp.cjs
*-tmp.js
*-tmp.mts
*-tmp.cts
*-tmp.ts
*-tmp.tsx
*-tmp.*.ts
*-tmp.json
*-tmp.html

# The real-design corpus: other people's design files, under their own terms. Never committed;
# extracted here (or pointed at with LOFT_CORPUS_DIR) so lib/corpus/sweep.test.ts can run. The
# suite skips itself when this is absent, so a public clone and a fork's CI stay green.
/corpus

# Vendored Pyodide + RocketPy runtime for the in-browser second solver (~40 MB).
# Regenerate with: node scripts/pyodide/vendor.mjs
/public/pyodide/
